      "message": "I\u0027m not sure which method you\u0027re referring to.\n\nThe method you highlighted in this comment is the instance method Parcel.hasFileDescriptors() (no-args). That method seems to scan the parcel for file-descriptors written, so I don\u0027t think that\u0027s actually using self-reported data from parcelables.\n\nOTOH, the static method I introduced in this class Parcel.hasFileDescriptors(Object) takes a \"value\" object and in most cases does use describeContents() to decide the answer. However, note that the CL is not a behavior change in this regard. I just moved this code out of bundle so that I could deal with LazyValue here (since now it became an implementation detail of parcel). I updated the javadoc to clarify where this information is coming from. Hope that\u0027s ok now.",
